Movement: Humans move at movement rate 9.

Damage dice: of the form <n>d<s>, where <n> is the number of dice to roll, and
<s> indicates the number of sides that die has.

Eat codes:
    A - Aggravates all monsters
    C - Confuses if eaten
    E - Gives ESP (detect nearby monsters if blind)
    F - Gives Fire Resistance
    H - Heals you to full hit points
    I - Confers ability to see invisible
    M - Mimic a treasure chest for a time
    P - Poisonous to eat, might cause death
    R - Turns you to rock, always
    RS- Confers Poison Resistance
    S - Sickening food, might cause loss of hit points
    T - Confers teleportation ability
    X - Gain an experience level

"To Hit" formula

    Base = 1d20
    Base = Base - Defender AC - Attacker Level
    if Defender confused, asleep, or frozen then Base = Base - 4
    if Base < 0 then the monster hit.

Special Attacks

    W - 1/3 chance of losing one point of strength
    F - 1/6 of the time breathes a 6d6 fireball at you
    P - 1/3 chance paralyzes you for 200(+) turns
    C - 6d6 points of frostbite damage, half damage if you duck
    S - Leprechauns steal money, Nymphs steal possessions
    E - Engulfs (swallows) you. Purple worms 25% chance, all others automatic
    R - Rusts helmet, then armor, then no damage
    PS- Poisons
    L - Lose an experience level
    A - 50% chance lose 1d6 points for acid damage
	17% chance weapon corrodes
	 2% chance armor corrodes
    RK- If it hits, you get turned to stone
    FZ- 17% chance of freezing you for 1d10 turns
    SL- 20% chance of sleeping you for 1d10 turns
    X - 11% chance of using back claws for 1d4/1d4
    H - Heals, and possibly increases max hit points, if carrying no armor
	or weapon.
    G - Grabs you for another 1d6, and does an automatic 2d8 this and every
	succeeding turn until dead.
    D - Often drops on you from above
    IM- Immobilizes you until dead
    SG- Segments might grow into new worms
    WN- Wounds legs, making it difficult to move
    L - Explodes into a ball of light, blinding you for 4d12 turns
    PM- Appears to be some other type of creature
    GT- 8% chance of creating another demon
    MM- Appears to be some type of object
